The WHO has issued instructions about when and how to use medical masks.
According to Steven Griffin, virologist at Leeds University, "the use of a medical mask can reduce people's propensity to touch their face, and touching the face with dirty hands is the main method of infection." Masks are also encouraged to use those who care for people who may be infected.
The World-Social World-General recommends that healthy people wear medical gummies only if they are at high-priority risk, such as people caring for someone with COVID-19, although it also recognizes the use of a mask, in fact, allows you to reduce touch to the face.
