Tests using the two-component components were not considered reliable until February 28, 2020, and it was only after this date that state and local laboratories were allowed to start testing.
The test was approved by the Food and Medications Supervisory Authority as part as part of an unencumbered permit for use. U.S. commercial laboratories began testing in the beginning of March in March 2020.
