Decreasing diarrhoea cases by 48% can be associated with handwash with soap. Washing hands with soap is the only most effective and inexpensive way to prevent diarrhoea and acute respiratorial diseases, provided that appropriate habits are developed in every home, in schools and other public places around the world.
Pneumonia, one of the main complications of ARI, is the leading cause of mortality among children under the age of five, which takes the lives of approximately 1.8 million children a year.
