Manufacturing Factors Control Connected with COVID-19
The control of industrial factors due to COVID-19 implies the use of methods to ensure the safety and protection of health in order to control risks and the fight against coronavirus in 2019 (COVID-19).
Appropriate risk control in the workplace depends on the location and work, based on risk assessment, the severity of the situation with the community epidemic and risk factors for individual workers, who may be vulnerable due to COVID-19.
Occupational Safety and Industrial Hygiene (OSHA) stated that positions with a lower level of risk have minimal professional contacts between the public and co-colleaquators, and in such cases requires basic measures to combat infection, including handwriting, encouraging workers to stay at home at disease, adherence to respiratory etiquette, as well as daily cleaning and disinfection of the working environment.
Modicated-risk positions require frequent or close contacts with people who do not have a confirmed or suspected COVID-19 diagnosis, but there is a possibility of injunction due to the current prevalence of the disease in society or during international trips.
This category can include workers in contact with the public, for example, in schools, high-decisive working environments and in some large retail stores.
Risk monitoring measures for such a group, in addition to the basic measures to prevent infection, include airing using high-performance air filters, the use of protective shields and available personal protective equipment in the event of contact with a person infected with COVID-19.
OSHA believes that medical and morgue employees who have come into contact with a person with a confirmed diagnosis or suspected COVID-to-COVID--19 are at a rate of high-risk; at the same time, the level of risk is increased to very high when such employees procedures accompanied by an aerosol formation, or collecting/processing samples from a person with a confirmed diagnosis or suspected COVID-19.
Risk control measures suitable for such employees include the use of engineering security tools, such as necessitated ventilation rooms, as well as personal protective equipment suitable for the task.
A COVID-19 flare can have various effects in the workplace.
Employees can be absent in the workplace in connection with their own illness, the need to take care of other persons or in connection with the fear of possible infection.
Commodity templates can be exchanged both in relation to the types of goods for which there is a demand, and the methods of acquiring such goods (for example, making purchases in non-fake periods with delivery or maintenance, not coming out of the machine).
At the end, there may be interruptions in the delivery of goods from the geographical regions affected by COVID-19. In the organization of the protection, you can use an epiphan-preparation and responsivestituation plan.
Supplies touches on issues about the risks associated with a variety of jobs and tasks, including sources of infection, risk factors arising at home and in communities, as well as risk factors for individual workers, such as old age or the presence of Chronic diseases.
The plans also specify the controls needed to deal with problems with such risks, as well as plans for emergency measures for situations that may arise as a result of an epidemic.
Immediate-family and responsive schemes can be subject to recommendations at the national or state level.
Some of the targets to respond to the epidemiological measure are to reduce the spread of the virus to staff, to protect people at a higher risk of serious health complications, maintain business operations and minimise the negative consequences for other organizations in their supply chains.
Responsive measures are influenced by the severity of diseases in the community where the business finds itself.
Hierarchy of risk controls is a structure widely used in the provision of safety and occupational health, for grouping such tools depending on the effectiveness.
If it is impossible to eliminate the risk of COVID-19 is the most effective engineering-technical means of safety, then - administrative measures and, at last, personal protective equipment.
The engineering and technical means of security implicity implication of Employees from job-to-risk sites and do not rely on the employee's behavior, which can be the most cost-effective solution.
Administrative measures involve a change in working policies or procedures that require action from an employee or employee.
Facilities of personal protection (PPE) are considered to be less effective compared with engineering or administrative measures, but can help to eliminate certain risks.
All types of means of personal protective equipment should be chosen depending on the threat to the employee, suitable in size (for example, respirators), be used constantly and properly, regularly checked, maintained in proper condition, and be replaced, as well as properly removed, purified and stored or disposed to avoid infection.
The U.S. Occupational and Industrial Hygiene (OSHA) Department of Occupation (OSHA) believes positions at the lowest risk have minimal contact with the public and their colleagues.
The basic anti-epidemic measures, recommended for all jobs, include frequent handwriting and thorough handwriting, recommendations for sick workers to stay at home, compliance with respiratory etiquette, including closing the oral shutdown by cough and sneezing, providing napkins and garbage containers, prepared for remote or removal, if necessary, recommendations for workers to avoid the use of other tools and equipment.
Prompt detection and issuing of individuals that can potentially be infected is a crucial step to protect Employees, customers, visitors and others in the workplace.
U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) recommend that employees with symptoms of spicy respiratory diseases stay at home until the cessation of helm, the absence of elevated body temper and many other symptoms for at least 24 hours without using antipyretics or other medications that eliminate symptoms, as well as to provide flexibility for the policy on hospital lists, to allow employees to stay at home to care for a sick family member.
According to OSHA, posts with a level level of risk require frequent and circulatory contacts at a distance of not more than six feet (1.8 m) with people who do not have confirmed data or suspicions of COVID-19 infection, but there is a possibility of SARS-CoV-2 in connection with the prevalence of the disease in a society where the business is located, or in connection with the recent trips of such a person to the distribution of COVID-19.
Such categories include workers who have been in contact with the public, for example, in schools, a working environment with a high-density of the population and certain large retail stores. The engineering and technical means of safety for such groups with higher risks include the installation of high-efficiency air filters, an increase in the intensity of ventilation, the installation of physical barriers, such as transparent plastic protective screens, and the installation of eyewitnesses for customer service.
In rare cases, employees at such a risk group may need respirators.
If a person fell ill on an airplane, then to ensure the proper safety of workers and other passengers, such measures are required to isolating a sick person from other people at a distance of 6 ot feet, the appointment of a crew member to care for a sick person, provide a sick mask or an appeal to such a person with a request to cover his nose and mouth with a napkin with a napkin during cough or sneezing.
Sentrifugal crew members should carry dispensing medical gloves when approaching a sick traveler or in contact with physiological fluids or potentially contaminated surfaces and, perhaps, additional personal protective equipment, if the patient has a fever, regular cough or difficulty with breathing.
Used gloves and other disposable objects should be placed in a biologically safe sack, and the contaminated surfaces must subsequently be cleaned and disinfected. In the cases of commercial navigation, including cruise liners and other passenger ships, the security measures include postponing a trip in the event of illness, self-isolation and immediately informing the medical center on the ship if there is a heat or other symptoms of someone on board.
Ideally, a medical examination should take place in an installed caus. In the case of schools and child-care facilities, CDC recommends short-term clusting for cleaning or disinfection if an infected person was in a school building, regardless of the prevalence of the disease in the community.
In the presence of a minimal or medium-sized level of the spread of infection in the communality, social distancing strategies can be introduced, for example, the cancellation of departures for face-to-face meetings, meetings and other mass events such as physical education or choral singing, eating food in cafeterias, increasing the distance between the desks, adjusting the time of arrival and care, limiting non-essential visits, the use of a separate location of health care institutions for children with flu symptoms.
At a significant rate of cilobism in the local community, in addition to social distancing strategies, measures for long-difficulty non-communication of the school can be considered. For law enforcement law enforcement officers performing daily responsibilities, the direct risk to health is considered low, according to the CDC.
Law Enforcement Employees who are obligmitted to contact persons with a confirmed diagnosis or suspected COVID-19 infection are advised to follow the same instructions prescribed to ambulance paramedics, including the use of suitable personal protective equipment.
If there is a close in contact in the course of detention, workers must purify and disinfect their formed belts and equipment before being reused using household cleaning aerosols or by rubbing, observe standard operating procedures to prevent the spread of the disease and the disposal of used personal protective equipment, as well as on the use and laundry of garments.
OSHA believes that certain categories of employees of health and morgue facilities are at a high or very high risk.
High-priced positions include medical, support officers, laboratory and medical personnel who come into contact with patients with a confirmed diagnosis or suspected COVID-19 infection.
They have a very high risk of contagion while carrying out procedures accompanied by an aerosol formation, or when sampling from persons with a confirmed diagnosis or suspected COVID-19 infection.
Procedures accompanied by an aerosol formation include sensitivization, cappitable, bronchoscopy, certain dental procedures and screenings or invasive sampling.
High-risk mbong workers include employees engaged in the processing of the bodies of persons with a confirmed disease or suspected COVID-19 at the time of their death; if such employees conduct an inauguration, then they are transferred to a category with a very high-priority category. Additional technical and technical safety equipment for such at-risk groups include the use of isolated premises for patients with a confirmed disease or suspected COVID-19.
In certain health and morgue institutions, an effective measure can be the use of special ventilation with negative pressure.
Sampls should be treated with the precautionary measures provided for the level of biological safety.
The World Health Organization (WHO) recommends distributing incoming patients to demarcated waiting areas, according to the presence of suspected COVID-19. Among other means of personal protection, OSHA recommends using respirators for workers interacting up to 6 vocabulary with patients with a confirmed disease or suspected SARS-CoV-2, as well as persons performing procedures accompanied by an aerosol.
In U.S. NIOSH respirators for a person with a N-95 or higher-priority filter need to be used as part of a comprehensive written respiratory respiratory program that specifies the requirements for individual retrieval and medical check-up.
Other types of respirators can provide more effective protection and comfort for an employee. WHO does not recommend the use of workwear, since COVID-19 is a disease transmitted respiratory, rather than through physiological fluids.
The WHO recommends using only surgical mascots for personnel performing screening at the point of admission of patients.
Persons collecting specimens from the respiratory tract in patients with COVID-19 or carriers of this disease without procedures accompanied by an aerosol formation, the WHO recommends wearing a surgical donkey, protective glasses, or protective screen for the face, coat and glove.
When carrying out the procedures accompanied by the formation of an aerosole, instead of a surgical masquerade, respirator N95 or FFP2 should be carried out.
Taking into account the insufficiency of personal protective equipment around the world, WHO recommends minimizing the need for such protective equipment due to the use of the capabilities of remote medicine, physical barriers, such so transparent wiages, providing access to a patient infected with COVID-19, only those persons who provide direct care, using only those means of personal protection that are necessary for a specific task, prolonged use of the same respirator, without removing, when dealing with several patients.
DEPUTY DEPUTY: Katherine Maher, Chief Executive Officer of the Wikimedia Foundation
REVIEWORS : Entire staff Wikimedia Foundation
TOPIC: [Covid-19] Promiscibility and preparation for the future
SHIMP TIME: March 14, 2020, 00:24 UTC
AUTHOUSED RESOLUENCE COMMISSARS: There Are No Secure Rights
We’re living in an unanimity this month.
The COVID-19 Epidemic is a phenomenon that sheaves a light on the interregnizance of people around the world and our calculus to each other.
There were no precedents for such problems, but we are aware that the effectiveness of our measures depends on the capacity to sympathize, co-operation and the development of communities around the world, which underlies such an organization.
We have witnessed a friendly and caring relationship between all our co-earners, which was reflected in electronic correspondence, calls and chat rooms - a wonderful confirmation of the fact that, fortunately, amazing people are working with us.
I am very grateful and vegetative to talk about you, as a colleague.
Last week I was informed about the appreciation of our work.
I’ve been reminded of how important it’s important for the world to address Wikipedia right right now, and how good it is for every person to have an online access to this key resource.
And this is possible thanks to your work, whether to ensure the opportunity of sites, payment to our co-colleagues or the protection of community security.
The world needs the information presented in Wikipedia, and today it is even more more important than never before.
At such a time to achieve significant results for the world, it is important not only what we are doing, but also how we do it.
Due to the importance of such a mission and your role in this process, we will introduce important changes in the order of our joint work, starting with the coming week.
Correction of the order of our work and schedules
As Robin used to say earlier, c-team team gathered last night to discuss our approach and schedule for the coming days and months.
In the course of communication, we looked upon our ideas on the most effective measures in the current situation and the best ways to ensure the stability of an organization during such a period.
The vast majority of of us wanted to relieve tensions and support our long-term mission.
if you want to back down, let it be.
For all personnel, contractors and free-staff employees:
according to our expectations, it will be necessary to work about 4 hours a day or 20 o'clock a week before subsequent orders are received.
We don’t announcing days off: If you can work normally for more hours, this is allowed for the purposes of our mission.
However, the world is unprepared right now; no matter what is your needs, whether caring for your relatives, buying food products or going to see a doctor, your well-being is our number one priority.
We don’t follow your working hours.
If you get sick, you don't have to work.
This is understandable and undeniable, but we mention it.
You do not need to issue a sick leave or time off: just inform your manager and help the team to revise the calendar and work schedule to ensure the coverage of key areas.
(If you’re diagnosed with COVID-19, let Bryan Bryan from T&C Ops so that T&C will be able to provide support and due diligence from management to your situation.
Hourly rates will be paid in full.
We have already pledged and reaffirm our intrusive commitment to our contractors and employees with an hour-of-creation rate.
Each person will receive payment according to the usual hourly bets, applied under normal circumstances.
This, in particular, impropens the periods of the disease, when you can not work.
If you want to work, we will support you.
Many people use work as a way of directing their efforts to the world around us.
What we are doing can bring amazing results, especially in such times.
Once again we are talking about self-help.
We are asking you to communicate with your supervisor so that we know what to expect, and we would be able to adjust our actions accordingly.
Certain types of work are considered significant.
We always need to support these activities.
SRE, HR Ops, Trust&Safety and Fundraising teams (in addition to others) are doing critical work that may require additional support.
We are innovating the process for all units to evaluate current targets and shift the emphasis on providing support, which is crucial for our mission.
There are many tasks for each of all of us, and we just focus on the most important projects.
Slowing today doesn't mean negative consequences in the future.
We don’t plan to work “twice as much to catch up” after the end of the pandemic.
You don’t need to work overtime to meet untrue deadlines for the current time.
We recognize that the circumstances have changed and we will work to set new goals and deadlines if possible.
What Happ (annorth plans)?
In order to adapt to a new apricot and awaiting the volume of daily working hours, we intend to adjust the deadline for the implementation of our annual plan for 2020-2021.
We intend to propose an extension of the deadline for our plan for 2019-2020, thus providing more time to form the budget, which will allow employees to give priority to critical work, self-help and caring for loved ones, and at the same time everyone who needs or who wants to work will be provided with a reduced schedule for the next few weeks.
Such an overdulfficiencies can significantly reduce the current pattern of planning and tension throughout the organization.
Next next week we will submit our proposal to the Council, inform representatives and teams up-to-date information on the next steps immediately after receiving the relevant confirmation.
Thank the APP team for the lead role in such a job.
Condition of the office, hazards and cleaning
Last week, we found out that one of our San Francisco colleagues may be infected with the COVID-19 virus.
However, in addition to many precautions, we hired an anti-virus cleaning team to disinfect all the surfaces in San Francisco.
They have used medical class antiviral solutions to disinfect all surfaces, as well as for the receiving and elevator lounges, through which it is possible to have access to our forlee.
In the building apply its own rules, prescribing caution, using products that ensure the safety of their tenants.
We feel that the office will be well-prepared for the period when we decide to come back.
Our office is located at WeWork, which has shared with us and all DC staff on DC related to COVID-19.
Last last week, our office in D.K. completely switched to remote work in accordance with instructions received in San’s San Francisco.
As we are aware of some of our colleagues from New York, we have also discussed the issue of renting premises in Brooklyn.
Such discussions are ongoing, but they can be postponed.
For the first time, some of our co-workers work remotely.
Our old co-colleagues who work remotely, are aware of the possibility of adjusting the situation and would like to give you some tips:
It is advisable to limit the duration of meetings to one or two hours.
If you need for longer severance sessions, consider the possibility of dislocating them into a course consisting of a few-three days.
Describe the purpose of the meeting, the agenda and silt materials in a predicate in advance.
By Default, use video communication to facilitate the interaction and communication, use tools such as Google Docs and Zoom.
For the sake of convenience, ascribe a coordinator - a person who will track the receipt of questions in the chat and control the list of speakers, as well as responsible for maintaining notes (or co-observation).
If it is necessary to use a comfortable headset, please contact the technical support service by e-mail.
Benefit Your Advantages of the Wellness Reimbursement program when buying snacks.
Join the #remonties in Slack to talk to colleagues about distributed work.
The HR Operations team examines ergonomy manuals available in webinar formats to facilitate the effectiveness of distributed work throughout the organization.
Last week, we asked all community grant recipients to rescue Wikimedia-financti-financient events such as editathons until the WHO announces an end to the pandemic.
We understand and communicate that our requests for such cancellations and other restrictions may result in the impossibility of holding agreed grant events, and no one will be penalized for forced delays or changing such objectives.
In the coming week, we will conduct follow-up events with additional instructions on Wikimania, as well as other regional and thematic community conferences.
Universal mood in the global community is not only frustration in connection with the interruption of the work, but also a certain sense of easing in connection with mutual understanding and the opportunity to focus on your own communities, Wikimedia and not only.
As for prospects, CRT is working on the Meta-Wiki page, which will provide a space for the community, which allows you to keep an eye on impact and communication.
We remain in contact on COVID-19-related
We will send an invitation to your calendar for a special staff meeting, which will take place next Thursday, 14:00 UTC/07:00 PT.
This time we will take the opportunity to additionally share up-to-date information, to answer your questions and spend time together, connecting to each other.
We are together in such a situation and we are ready to help with everything we can.
In this case you can continue to receive information from such electronic correspondence, and other important information on COVID-19 from Office Wiki.
CRT will update such pages, and all information will be compiled in one place.
We are also working to maintain regular communication with personnel living in countries that have been significantly affected by the current situation.
If there are questions about trips, events, a key workflow, problems with the coverage of the information or, if you need other assistance, please contact CRT.
We are ready to provide support and provide communication as necessary.
In the presence of problems associated with confidentiality, please contact Bryan Judan, Director of HR International Global Operations.
Such changes should not be constituted as a renunciation of our work and our obligations.
Rather, on the contrary: it is the recognition of the possible current need for a fundamentally new adaptation of our work and obligations.
We believe that such steps are necessary to support each other and to provide an opportunity to continue to work, to provide the necessary support to our movement and the whole world with the right service.
Our planned work will wait until relevant times.
It’s time to support each other and create a space for the important work going on next few weeks and possibly months.
In order for this to happen, we will need help from every one of you; and we need you to take care of yourself and your families, as well as work with maximum dedication, as soon as such a need arises.
And now please wash your hands and don’t touch your face.
Katherine, CRT (Amanda K, Amy V, Bryan J, Doreen D, Gregory V, Jaime V, Joel L, Lynette L, Ryan M, Tony S), and other members of the Leadership Team (Grant I, Heather W, Jaime V, Janen U, Lisa S, Robyn A, Ryan M, and Toby N).
Angiotenzin-converting enzyme 2 (ACE2) is an enzyme attached to the external surface (cenal membranes) of cells in the lungs, arteries, the heart, kidneys and integument.
ACE2 antiposes the activity of the corresponding angiotensin-concreting enzyme (ACE), reducing the angiotensin-II and increasing Ang (1-7), making it a promising solution for the treatment of cardiovascular diseases.
The human version of the enmity is often referred to as hACE2.
Angiotensin-conspiring enzyme 2 is a zinc-containing screefinance located on the surface of endothelial and other cells.
Protein ACE2 Concludes an N-final peptidase domain M2 and the C-capital transport domain of renal amino acid collectrin.
ACE2 is a single-entrance membrane protein of type I, its enemplatively active domain enters the surface of the cells of the lung and other fabrics.
Extracellular domain ACE2 cleavages from the transmembrane domain by another enzyme, known as shedase, and the resulting solvable squirrel is released into the bloodstream and eventually excreted in the urinary.
ACE2 is present in most organs: ACE2 is attached to the cell membrane of most lung alveolary cells of type II, thin intestinal enterocytes, arterial and venous endothelial cells and cells of the glened muscles of the arteries of the arteries of most organs.
Biosynthesis of ACE2 iRPN is also found in the cerebral cortex, striatum, hypothalamus, and cerebral sterbum.
The main function of ACE2 is to act as an ACE counterbalancing.
ACE breaks the hormone angiothenzine I into vascular angiotensin II.
ACE2, in turn cleaves the carboxyl terminal amino acid phenylalanine from angiotensin II (Asp-Arg-Val-Ty-Tysle-His-Pro-Phe) and hydroplifies it into vasodilator angiotensin (1–7).
ACE2 can also schelate a number of other peptides, including [des-Arg9] -bradicin, apelin, neurotensin, dinorphine A and ghrelin.
ACE2 also regulates the memabranic transport of the neutral amino ambigs transmitter SLC6A19 and is present in Hartnupa.
Being a transmembranic protein, ACE2 serves as the main entry point of cells for some coronaviruses, including HCoV-NL63; SARS-CoV (SARS-COV virus); and SARS-CoV-2 (a virus causing COVID-19).
Strict-to-speak, the bindling the SARS-CoV adhesue protein S1 and SARS-CoV2 with the enzymatic ACE2 domain on the cell surface leads to endocycytosis and translocation of a virus and an enzyme into endosomes located inside the cells.
This inbounding process also requires premisating the S serine protease protease of TMPRS2, whose inhibition is currently being studied as a potential therapeutic agent. This has led some to the idea that a decrease in ACE2 levels in the cells can help in the fight against the infection.
Nevertheless, many professional communities and regulators are advised to continue the standard APF and BRA inhibitor therapy.
According to a systematic review and meta-examination published on July 11, 2012 “the use of APF inhibitors was associated with a significant decrease in pneumonia risk by 34% compared to the control group”.
What’s more, “Pneumonia risk has also been lowered in patients receiving APF inhibitors who were at a higher risk of pneumonia, especially patients with stroke and cardiac insufficiency.
The use of APF inhibitors was also associated with a decrease in pneumonia mortality, although the results were less reliable than in patients with a general risk of pneumonia.”
Recombinant human ACE2 (rhACE2) is believed to be an innovate for acute pulmonary lesions and seems to improve pulmonary hemodynamics and saturation of hydrops in piglets in pigs with acute respiratory insufficient insufficiency syndrome caused by lipopolysaccharides.
The half-excrepancy period rhACE2 in people is about 10 hours, and the onset of action is 30 minutes, in addition to the duration of exposure at 24 hours.
Some evidence suggests that rhACE2 can become a promising agent for people with intolerance to classic renin-angiotisen system inhibitors (RAS inhibitors) or in diseases where circulating angiothenine II has been increased.
COVID-19 applications are software applications for mobile phones, designed to assist in an epidemiological investigation of the coronavirus pandemic of 2019-20, i.e. the identification of persons (“contacts”) who were able to come into contact with an infected person.
In some regions, many applications have been developed or proposed, officially supported by the authorities.
A number of options have been developed for contact tracking applications.
This sprooked a discussion about privacy issues, especially with regard to those systems that are based on tracing the geographical location of application users.
Tanger options in this regard include the use of Bluetooth signals to register the user's closeness to other mobile phones.
On April 10, 2020, Google and Apple announced that they would combine their efforts to integrate the functionality of supporting such applications based on Bluetooth directly into their Android and iOS operating systems.
In China, the government, together with Alipay, has unfurloped an app, which allows citizens to check whether they communicated with people infected with COVID-19.
It is used in more than 200 Chinese cities. In Singapore, an application called TraceTogether is used.
The application was developed by local IT companies, has an open-source code and will be transferred to the government. North Macedonia has launched the “StopKorona!” application, working on Bluetooth, which helps track contacts with potentially infected people and provides operational links with health authorities.
The application was co-developed by the Ministry of Communications and Technology and the Ministry of Health.
As of April 14, 2020, the app was awaiting registration with the Google Play Store and the Apple App Store.
On April 12, the government stated that the contact tracing app is at the final stage of development and will be available for deployment within a number of weeks. Similar applications are planned to be launched in Ireland and in France ("StopCovid").
Australia and New Zealand are looking forward to the use of applications based on the Singapore TraceTogether application and the BlueTrace protocol. Russia intends to use the application with a geozoning function, the purpose of which is to ensure that patients diagnosed with COVID-19, living in Moscow, do not leave their homes.
Ross Anderson, a professor of security at the University of Cambridge, outlines a number of potential practical problems that can arise with application-based systems, including false impact and potential inefficiencies in the case of using an application only a small part of the population.
Taking into account concerns about the cilobization of misleading or malicious “coronavirus” applications, Apple has limited a list of types of organizations that can offer their coronavirus-related applications in the App Store, including only “familiarily” or other trustworthy organizations.
“Mooker and Amazon have also introduced similar restrictions.
The participants of the privacy campaign expressed concern about the consequences of mass monitoring of the population through applications related to the coronavirus; in particular, the question was raised as to be dismantled the surveillance infrastructure created to combat the coronavirus pandemic when the threat will be dismantled.
Amnesty (International Amnesty” and more than 100 other organizations issued a statement calling for the restriction of this type of supervision.
The organizations announced the eight conditions imposed by them for state projects:
Observation should be “legitimate, necessary and proportionate”;
Expansion of monitoring and follow-up should be accompanied by time-constitutional reservations;
the use of the data should be limited to the anticipation of COVID-19;
security and an anonymity of the data must be protected, and there should be evidence of such security.
Digital surveillance should preclude exacerbation of disparities and marginalization;
any exchange of data with third parties should be determined at the level of the legislation;
should guarantee protection against abusions, as well as the right of citizens to respond to abuse;
“Measbative participation” should be ensured by “relevant stakeholders”, including public health experts and representatives of marginalized groups. The German Chaos Computer Club (CCC) and reporters Without Borders (Reporter ohne Grenzen (RSF) have also published their lists of conditions.
Google and Apple are proposing a joint plan to solve the problem of constant surveillance, which consists in the removal of the tracking mechanism from the operating systems of their devices, as soon as the need disappears.
In some countries, network location tracking is used instead of applications, which precludes the need to load the application and the ability to avoid tracking.
In Israel, network tracking has been approved.
Network solutions, which have access to the original location data, also have large potential privacy issues.
However, not all systems with central servers should have access to personal location data; a number of privacy-by-preserving systems have been developed, which use central servers for communication only (see section below).
In South Korea, a system was used to track contacts that does not use applications as a basis.
Instead of using a special application, the system collected tracing information from a variety of sources, including tracking data from mobile devices and card transactions, and then combined them to create notifications in the form of text messages, which were sent to potentially infected individuals.
The government not only used this information to warn citizens about potential contacts with infected persons, but also made information about the whereabouts publicly available, which became possible due to significant changes in information security legislation that were made after the MERS outbreak in that country.
Access to such information can be obtained through a number of applications and websites. Countries, including Germany, are considering the use of both centralized systems and systems that preserve confidentiality.
As of April 6 in 2020, the details have not yet been made public.
Contiguring contact tracking, in which confidentiality persists – a well-established concept, a significant volume of research literature on which is dated at least in 2013. As of April 7, 2020, more than ten expert groups have been working on solutions that provide privacy, such as using Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) to register a user approximation to other mobile phones.
PEPP-PT, however, is a product of coordination efforts, which includes both centralized and decentralized approaches, and it is not a single protocol. Decentralized protocols include decentralized privacy tracing (DP-PPT/DP-3T), temporary contact numbers (TCN, fka EventNumbers, CEN), protocols to provide privacy, mobile contact tracking (PACT) and others.
These protocols are responsible so that identifiable personal data will never leave the device, and all the comparisons took place on it.
MIT Media Lab is engaged in the development of Safe Paphths, a platform that preserves confidentiality when collecting and using location data or intersiping paths to track the proliferation of COVID-19.
The work of this platform is based on the research set out in “Apps Gone Rogue: Maintaining Personal Privacy in an Epidemic”, published in March 2020.
SafeTrace uses reliable hardware technologies that allow users to exchange confidential location and health data with other users and officials without jeopardizing the confidentiality of this data.
On April 5, 2020, groups separating the Same Approach and using similar protocols were founded by the global coalition of TCN to reduce the fragmentation and global interoperability of tracing and notification applications, which is a key factor in their widespread dissemination.
On April 9, 2020, the government of Singapore announced that it had opened the BlueTrace source code used in its official application.
On April 10, 2020, Google and Apple, companies that are monitoring the operation of mobile platforms Android and iOS, announced a contact tracking initiative, which they claimed would provide privacy, which is based on a combination of Bluetooth Low Energy technology and cryptography that allows you to maintain privacy.
They also published the technical characteristics of the main technologies used in the operation of the system.
According to the data of Apple and Google, the system should be deployed in three stages:
Deployment of tools to enable governments to create official applications to track the movement of coronavirus-infected citizens, but while maintaining the confidentiality
Improving this functionality directly in iOS and Android, Google and Apple plan to solve problems with constant surveillance, first introducing the system through the updates of the operating system, and then deleting it in the same way after the threat has disappeared.
Reposting a medicinal product (also known as reprofiling, redirecting, changing tasks or therapeutic redividing of drugs) is a reprofilation of an approved drug for the purpose of treating a disease or a medical condition other than a disease originally provided for in development.
This is one of the directions of scientific research, which is currently being used to develop safe and effective methods of treating COVID-19.
Other areas of the study include the development of a COVID-19 vaccine and transfusion of convasequente plasma. SARS-CoV-2 contains about 66 proteins that are appointed to drugs, each of which has several ligand-binding areas.
Analyzing of these binding sites serves as a suitable basis for the development of an effective antiviral drug against COVID-19 protein.
The most important trimming squirrels for SARS-CoV-2 - papain-like protease, RNA-dependent RNA polymerase, helicase, protein S and ADP-ribophosphatase.
Hussein AA and co-collemen in their preclinical study examined several candidate compounds, which were then optimized and analysed their resemblance according to the structure with the most similar approved drugs to accelerate the development of a highly effective drug against SARS-CoV-2, which will be recommended for clinical trials.
Khloroquine is an anti-malarial drug, which is also used in the treatment of certain autoimmune diseases.
On March 18, WHO announced that chloroquine and associated hydroxychloroquine will be one of the four drugs investigated as part of the Solidarity Clinical Trial.
New York Governor Andrew Cuomo announced that chloroquine and hydroxychloroquine tests will begin in the state of New York on March 24. On March 28, the FDA authorized the use of hydroxychloroquine sulphate and chloroquine phosphate in accordance with an emergency use (EUA).
The treatment regimen has not been approved by the FDA clinical trial and is allowed according to the EUA only as an experimental treatment for emergency care in patients who have been hospitalized but cannot be treated according to clinical trial schemes.
CDC stated that “the order of use, dosing, or duration of taking hydroxychloroquine to prevent or treat SARS-CoV-2 infection hasn’t been established yet.
Physicians say that they are using the drug when “there is no other way out.”
The Turkish research team in Istanbul is conducting a small study on chloroquine using chlorochin combined with zinc and vitamins A, C and D.
Large-Scale studies are conducted at the University of Duke and the University of Oxford.
New York University Medical School in Langone studies the safety and efficacy of hydroxychloroquine.
Chinese clinical trials in Wuhan and Shenzhen have shown favipiravir “unambiguously effective”.
In 35 patients in Shenzhen, who took this drug, a negative result was obtained on an an average of after 4 days, while in 45 patients who did not take the drug, the duration of the disease amounted to 11 days.
In Wuhan conducted a study that monitored 240 patients with pneumonia, one half of whom received favipiravir, and the other half - umifenovir.
The Italian Pharmaceutical Agency reminded the public that the results indicating the efficacy of the drug are scarce and should not be considered conclusive.
On April 2, Germany announced that to replenish its reserves will purchase the drug in Japan, and for its delivery to university hospitals, where the drug will be used to treat patients with COVID-19 will use military resources.
According to the newspaper South China Morning Post, Shinzo Abe told the Trump administration about the possibility of purchasing the drug. The drug may be less effective in advanced cases of the disease.
Its use may be unsatisfactory for pregnitant patients or for patients who are attempting to get pregnitute.
According to the results of one study devoted to the combination of antiviral drugs "lopinovir" and "ritonavir" (Cathera), it was concluded that "the effectiveness of the use of drugs has not been identified."
Medications were designed to inhibate HIV replication by linking protease.
A group of researchers from the University of Colorado tries to modify drugs in order to find a compound that will be associated with SARS-CoV-2 protease. The scientific community criticizes the reprofiling of drugs that were specially developed for the treatment of HIV and AIDS.
The WHO has included a combination of Lopinavir and Ritonavir in an international solidarity test.
Remdesivir was created and engineered by Gilead Sciences to treat the Ebola virus and marburg viral infections. Subsequently, Gilead Sciences employees found that remdesivir has antiviral activity in vitro against a set of phylos, pneumatic, paramix and coronavirus.
