The coronavirus is a disease detected in 2019 (COVID-19), which is an infectious disease caused by severe acute respiratory coronavirus syndrome 2 (SARS-CoV-2).
The most prevalent symptoms include fever, cough, and breathing difficulties.
Other symptoms may include a feeling of fatigue, muscle arrears, diarrhea, sore throats, laryngeal loss and abdominal abdominal abdominal abdominal pain.
The period from the first manifestation of symptoms to the peanen of the disease is usually about five days, but it can also vary from two to fourteen days.
The majority of cases are reduced to the manifestation of mild symptoms, but in some cases the disease flows into viral pneumonia and organ failure.
As of April 17, 2020, more than 2.24 million infections were recorded in 210 countries and regions, more than 153 000 people died from the disease.
more than 568 000 people have recovered. The virus mainly spreads when people communicate closely with each other, often through microscopic drops excreting into the air during cough, sneezing or talking.
Although these droplets are formed by excretion, they usually pose a threat, falling to the ground or on the surface, but are not transmitted through the air at great distances.
People also become infected, touching the polluted surface and then their eyes, nasal, or moron.
On the surface, the virus can live for 72 o'clock.
It is most contagious during the first three days after the onset of symptoms, although its propagation may be possible both before the oncoming symptoms and in the later stages.
The use of medical masks is recommended for patients with suspected the disease, as well as those who take care of them.
Recommendations on the use of medical masks by the population are different: some departments recommend not to use them at all, some recommend their use, while others demand it.
At the present time there is a vaccine or specific treatment for the COVID-19 virus.
The local spread of the disease has been recorded in most countries in all six regions of WHO.
Influenced individuals may have no symptoms of influenza, such as a fever, cough, fatigue, and shortness of breath.
Urgency symptoms include difficulty-breeding, constant pain or a feeling of compression in the chest, entanglement of consciousness, waking, bruising or pulmonary; if the above symptoms are present, you should immediately seek medical help.
Less often there may be symptoms of upper respiratory tract disease, such as sneezing, runaway or sore throat.
Also, in different interest rates, gastrointestinal symptoms such as nausea, vomit and diarrhoea.
Some cases of the disease registered in China were initially manifested only by a feeling of compression in the chest and probable heartbeat.
In some cases, the disease can progress, developing into pneumonia, organ insufficiency, and eventually death occurs.
It’s called an incubation period.
Incubation period COVID-19 is usually five to six days, but can vary from two to 14 days.
In 97.5% of people, the symptoms begin to appear within 11.5 days after the influenvironment. According to available data, the symptoms do not manifest themselves in all those who are infected.
Such asymptomatic carriers is still fully unreleased, but preliminary data indicate that they can contribute to the spread of infection.
The percentage of infected people with an asymptomobile course of the disease is currently unidentified, it's only being studied, while Korean Centers for Disease Control and Disease Insufficiency (KCDC) reported that in 20 percent of all confirmed cases and hospitalizations for the virus disease was asymptomatic asymptomatic.
The National Health Commission of China began including asymptocellant cases in its daily report from April 1; of the 166 cases of infection registered on this day, 130 (78%) refused asymptomatic at the time of testing.
