The disease can occur in a mild form with insignificant or missing symptoms resembling other common diseases of the upper respiratory uterus, such as an ordinary cold.
Patients with a mild form of the disease get healed, as a rule, for two weeks, while it may take from three to six weeks to treat patients with severe or critical forms.
