In persons with the most severe course of COVID-19, COVID-19 can progress rapidly into acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), causing respiratory insufficiency, septic hypotaste, or polyorganic insufficiency.
Complications of COVID-19 include sepsis, anomalous thrombosis, as well as problems with the heart, bundles and the liver.
Anomalies of thrombosis, especially an enlargement of prothrombin time, were described in 6% of patients enrolled with COVID-19, while impatisfaction of renal function is observed in 4% of this group.
Approroximately 20-30% of patients with COVID-19 elevated liver enzymes (transaminases).
