It is believed that in these cases an exacerbated prolonged course of the disease took place, and not a repeated infection.
It is believed that the virus is considered to be a naturally occurring animal origin and is an infectious disease.
The actual origin of the virus is unknown, but by December of 2019 the spread of the infection was almost completely due to its transfer from a person to a person.
A study of the first 41 confirmed COVID-19, Published in January 2020 in The Lancet, called December 1, 2019 the earliest date of the first case.
